# Line-ending law for a mixed-OS team. Every text file is stored AND checked
# out with LF, overriding any local core.autocrlf (git on Windows defaults it
# to true). Without this, a Windows-side clone rewrites the shell scripts to
# CRLF and they die in the containers with "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Auto-detection already treats these as binary; being explicit costs nothing
# and protects against a misdetected edge case.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
